completed_at: "2026-09-07T07:45:36.395Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Grouping by a set-valued field groups by element: --group-by tags returns one row per distinct tag with the count of items carrying it, and an item with k tags contributes to k rows; The tuple behaviour remains reachable under an explicit spelling if it has a use, and is documented as a distinct operation rather than as the default reading of the field name; The row-count expansion is bounded and the declared ceiling is honoured; The rule for every present and future set-valued field is declared once rather than per field; The 182 untagged closed items are measured as a named population with a disposition"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: 93
resolution: "Implemented distinct-member aggregation with explicit tuple compatibility, unique-item versus membership totals, complete strict input reads, and bounded group pagination across SDK/CLI/MCP contracts."
expected_result: "Every set member contributes once to its group; default output stays bounded without truncating the input population, and historical absence remains visible."
actual_result: Real 10000-item regression counts the full corpus before returning 50 of 61 groups and the remaining 11 on continuation. Numeric membership and tuple acceptance pass. Live closed-item census measured 218 untagged items among 2362 closed records; these remain an explicit null population without invented tags. Contract-summary output measured 4108 tokens within the unchanged 4111 ceiling.
