comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-07T06:11:51.972Z","harness:codex","Implementation design: default set-element grouping with one contribution per distinct member; explicit tuple mode preserves legacy grouping; scalar dimensions compose with member grouping; untagged population remains an explicit null group. Tests precede implementation."
  "2026-09-07T06:24:16.366Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: initial regression suite passes locally; integration, additional edge cases, full coverage and release/review gates remain underway. No delivery or release completion claimed."
  "2026-09-07T06:30:05.245Z","harness:codex","Integration finding: aggregate inherited list automatic item pagination at 10,000 rows, which could undercount large workspaces. Aggregate now requests a strict complete input read, then applies bounded group pagination with an explicit cursor. This is part of the same canonical aggregation correctness and output-bound lineage."
  "2026-09-07T06:48:01.074Z","harness:codex","Live acceptance census: strict aggregation over all 2362 closed items produced 1077 member groups and 9920 memberships; 218 closed items are in the explicit (untagged) population, rather than the older 182-item snapshot. Disposition: retain historical absence faithfully as a named null group; do not invent retrospective tags. Future enrichment should use evidenced historical categories. Aggregation CLI adds precisely three controls (set-mode, limit, after), with the flag-count declaration updated and help text tightened to preserve the existing help-token ceiling."
  "2026-09-07T07:11:57.888Z","harness:codex","Packed installed acceptance passed with separate npm and Bun roots and runtimes: CLI group pagination and tuple mode, SDK numeric membership aggregation, and MCP pm_run action=aggregate. The 10000-item filesystem regression proves complete population counting before the default 50-group page. Contracts discovery surfaced the new limit/after flags at +7 tokens; two redundant intent phrases were shortened to absorb that growth without changing the agent-task budget."
  "2026-09-07T07:12:50.371Z","harness:codex","Acceptance scope clarification: installed npm/Bun CLI, SDK, and MCP acceptance exercised element-mode pagination; tuple compatibility is separately proven by the linked SDK/CLI regression suite, which now passes 15 targeted tests together with deadline and lifecycle cases."
  "2026-09-07T07:23:02.508Z","harness:codex","Verification update: all linked aggregation tests passed. Full coverage identified that subprocess CLI acceptance does not instrument the parent adapter; the real tuple SDK acceptance now consumes normalizeAggregateOptions directly as well. Discovery descriptions are tightened further to preserve the unchanged context budget. Concurrent build outputs caused two benchmark process failures; verification is being rerun with build steps serialized and immutable outputs during tests."
  "2026-09-07T07:45:35.802Z","harness:codex","Local implementation verification: exact full-source coverage passed at 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts (60671 lines, 63170 statements, 13078 functions, 47962 branches). The full run had one stale workspace-intent assertion; that expected text was synchronized, then all 55 contracts and aggregation acceptance tests passed. Full static quality, context-quality and 56 token surfaces, typecheck, linked tests, staged secret scan, latest-release compatibility migration, 88-command package dogfood, installed npm/Bun CLI/SDK/MCP acceptance, and packed npx/bunx smoke passed. Hosted exact-head review, merge, and publication remain separate delivery steps; no hosted or released state is claimed here."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-07T07:26:14.590Z","harness:codex","Membership totals and distinct item totals answer different questions. Read the complete input before paging groups, and retain missing historical categorization as an explicit population instead of fabricating tags."
